00:56:34.490 --> 00:56:38.729
Serhan Dagtas: To spend a few minutes and to actually,

526
00:56:40.520 --> 00:56:46.109
Serhan Dagtas: Answer the questions in the survey, so there may be other ways, of course.

527
00:56:46.250 --> 00:56:49.910
Serhan Dagtas: to incentivize the process.

528
00:56:50.230 --> 00:57:01.269
Serhan Dagtas: And of course this in general is found to improve the response rates. Not just the rate itself, but also it may improve the response quality.

529
00:57:01.450 --> 00:57:07.489
Serhan Dagtas: When people are, you know, need some favors.

530
00:57:07.670 --> 00:57:09.709
Serhan Dagtas: They may be more careful.

531
00:57:10.080 --> 00:57:12.840
Serhan Dagtas: And providing more accurate.

532
00:57:13.070 --> 00:57:17.180
Serhan Dagtas: responses to… This survey.

533
00:57:18.300 --> 00:57:26.620
Serhan Dagtas: Obviously, this should not sacrifice the quality of the survey or the quality of the responses.

534
00:57:28.170 --> 00:57:28.880
Serhan Dagtas: Good.

535
00:57:31.040 --> 00:57:31.700
Serhan Dagtas: Pretty good.

